            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>4</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>10</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>0</m>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </table>
      </statement>
    <answer><m>1</m></answer>
  </exercise>

   <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=x^2+16</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=1</m> to <m>x=10</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>11</m></answer>
  </exercise>

     <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>g(x)</m> is given in the table below. Compute the average rate of change of <m>g(x)</m> from <m>x=1</m> to <m>x=7</m>. </p>
     <table>
        <tabular top="medium">
          <row left="medium" bottom="medium">
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>x</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>1</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>3</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>5</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>7</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>15</m>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row left="medium" bottom="medium">
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>g(x)</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>10</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>2</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>14</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>21</m>
            </cell>
            <cell right="medium">
              <m>0</m>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </table>
      </statement>
    <answer><m>\frac{11}{6}</m></answer>
  </exercise>

 <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=3x-7</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=-5</m> to <m>x=-2</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>3</m></answer>
  </exercise>

<exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)</m> is given in the graph below. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=0</m> to <m>x=4</m>.</p>
      <image source="Functions/PracExercise1.png"/>
      </statement>
    <answer><m>1</m></answer>
  </exercise>

   <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=x^2-21</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=3</m> to <m>x=5</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>8</m></answer>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=x^2-2</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=1</m> to <m>x=1+h</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>2+h</m></answer>
  </exercise>

   <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=3x^2 +2x</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=2</m> to <m>x=2+h</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>3h+10</m></answer>
  </exercise>

   <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=10x+2</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=a</m> to <m>x=a+h</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>10</m></answer>
  </exercise>

   <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=x^2 +4x +4</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=a</m> to <m>x=a+h</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>h+2a+4</m></answer>
  </exercise>

   <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=x^2+25</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=5</m> to <m>x=5+h</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>10+h</m></answer>
  </exercise>

 <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=-x^2-3x+1</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=a</m> to <m>x=a+h</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>-2a-h+3</m></answer>
  </exercise>

   <exercise>
  <statement><p>Suppose <m>f(x)=2x^2+10x</m>. Compute the average rate of change of <m>f(x)</m> from <m>x=3</m> to <m>x=3+h</m>.</p></statement>
    <answer><m>2h+22</m></answer>
  </exercise>

</exercises> 
</chapter>
